WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.170
- [Narrator] There are a lot of us

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:09.170
all with different cultures,
languages, beliefs.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.430
So, yeah. Communication.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.730
It's not always easy.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:13.563
- You're crazy

00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:14.396
- You're crazy

00:00:14.396 --> 00:00:15.229
- You're crazy

00:00:15.229 --> 00:00:16.130
(slapping)

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.780
- [Narrator] But no
matter where we come from

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.550
or the languages we speak

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.390
by using these,

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.820
we can still connect with other humans.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.263
And now maybe with them too.

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.697
- There are so many purposes
of facial expressions.

00:00:32.697 --> 00:00:34.610
I'm David Matsumoto.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:35.930
I'm a Professor of Psychology

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:37.770
at San Francisco State University,

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.860
and I'm also director of Humintell.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.940
The face is one of the
most complex signal systems

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.390
we have in the body.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.280
And it serves many purposes.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:50.800
For example, when we wrinkle
our nose in disgust like this,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.970
not only is it communicating
something to you

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:54.670
who can perceive my expression,

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.990
what is also doing is

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.780
clamping down a little bit
on those nasal passages.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.560
It's preventing things
from coming into my body,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.810
through my nasal passage.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.610
- [Narrator] Facial
expressions also communicate

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.260
to the people around us.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:10.660
One of the biggest
advocates for this theory,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.910
Charles Darwin.

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.683
- [David] Darwin posited that
all humans have emotions.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.420
It allows us to act immediately

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.980
with minimal conscious
thinking or awareness.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.600
And then on top of that,

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.470
we add these expressions

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:30.140
so that we could communicate that reaction

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.580
to others as well

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.993
and that helped the group to survive.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.293
- [Narrator] Because of this,

00:01:36.293 --> 00:01:39.030
Darwin believed our expressions were

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:39.863
universal.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.580
- So in psychology today,

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.600
there is widespread agreement

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.970
that seven facial expressions of emotion

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.830
are universally recognized
all around the world,

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.550
regardless of race, color,
creed, nationality, gender,

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.940
any demographic that exists.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:58.830
They are

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:03.830
anger, contempt, disgust,
fear, happiness, sadness,

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.686
and surprise.

00:02:05.686 --> 00:02:08.436
(dramatic music)

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.330
- [Narrator] So this means as humans,

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:14.680
we can talk to each other,

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:15.969
even without words

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:19.330
(dramatic music)

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.040
But can facial expressions

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.543
help us connect with
human-like technology?

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.510
- So the robot is a way to
understand human self, for me.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.640
By creating the very human-like robot

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.913
I believe that we can get some
knowledge about the humans.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:37.720
My name is Hiroshi Ishiguro.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.030
I'm a roboticist.

00:02:40.401 --> 00:02:44.540
What I could learn through the robots

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.548
so many things, right?

00:02:45.548 --> 00:02:50.053
We are trying to develop
interacting robots with humans.

00:02:51.521 --> 00:02:54.271
(dramatic music)

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.130
And we're studying the how the human

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.200
can interact with the robots.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.251
So in order to develop
that kind of a robot

00:03:04.251 --> 00:03:06.217
the first facial expressions

00:03:06.217 --> 00:03:07.370
and the gazing directions

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.353
gazing control of the
robot is so very important.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:15.500
So robot needs to represent the emotions

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.453
and intelligence in many ways.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.368
We have totally different cultures

00:03:23.368 --> 00:03:25.500
between United States and in Japan,

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.880
but I know that we understand
emotional expression.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.420
There is no doubt emotional
facial expressions

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.620
is a very important way of communication.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.737
So therefore the facial
expression is very important

00:03:38.737 --> 00:03:42.393
for android and for having
the communication with human.

00:03:46.027 --> 00:03:46.860
- [Robot] Hello,

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.400
My name is Erica.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.140
- [Robot] Meet Erica.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:54.610
- I think Erica is the most
human like android in the world.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:58.300
Erica can have a kind of
a natural conversation

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:00.330
with the visitors.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.813
Maybe the five or 10 minutes.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.486
We are implementing the, maybe just major

00:04:07.486 --> 00:04:10.078
the facial expression with Erica.

00:04:10.078 --> 00:04:10.980
Happy,

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.460
- It's all very exciting

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.293
- Angry.

00:04:13.293 --> 00:04:14.453
- I'm done talking to you,

00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:17.789
please don't come speak with me again.

00:04:17.789 --> 00:04:20.647
- And it's sad and depressed.

00:04:20.647 --> 00:04:23.564
(foreign language)

00:04:25.105 --> 00:04:29.030
- So Android can have their communications

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.200
by exchanging the facial expressions

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:34.780
even if android doesn't
understand the language.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.250
- There are so many great
applications for these robots.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.400
Whether it's helping the
elderly, guiding tourists

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.730
or even for entertainment.

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.063
It's all very exciting.

00:04:43.807 --> 00:04:46.680
Oh, sorry about that.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.403
I got a little carried away.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.810
- [Narrator] By designing robots
to have facial expressions,

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.120
humans could more easily connect with them

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.460
and incorporate them into our lives.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.963
- It's just really interesting because

00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:03.670
we use our faces to reference
many different mental states.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.260
- By expressing the facial expression.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.534
Even if we don't understand
our language to each other,

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:13.410
we can the share some information.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.890
- And because of that facial
expressions of emotion are

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:19.290
the closest thing we have
to a universal language.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:23.020
They allow us to share
emotions with each other.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.310
They allow us to share the time

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:28.253
when we laugh together or cry together.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.680
If there's anything out there,

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.130
they're the single most important vehicle

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.330
that we have that can
bring us all together.

00:05:36.051 --> 00:05:38.634
(upbeat music)

